    "result_text": "The build passes and the test is green. Let me verify the audit log confirms the fiscal-year behavior is working end-to-end \u2014 the earlier run showed `membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M26` for `registrationDate=2026-09-17`, which is correct: 2026-09-17 is on/after 1 July, so it falls in FY26.\n\nThe change is complete. Here's what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\nMoved date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts **1 July**, labelled `FY<YY>` by its starting calendar year's last two digits).\n\n**New helper \u2014 `FiscalYear.java`** (model package): the single source of truth for turning a date into a fiscal year.\n- `startingYearOf(date)` \u2014 the calendar year the containing fiscal year begins in.\n- `shortYearOf(date)` \u2014 that year's last two digits (the identifier segment).\n- `labelFor(date)` \u2014 the `FY<YY>` label.\n- `elapsedBetween(from, to)` \u2014 whole fiscal years crossed (used for tenure).\n\n**`Tenure.java`** \u2014 now counts tenure in **elapsed fiscal years** instead of 365-day windows. `qualifiesForTopLevel` delegates to `FiscalYear.elapsedBetween` and requires more than one fiscal year (`QUALIFYING_FISCAL_YEARS = 1`).\n\n**`Owner.java`**\n- `getMembershipNumber()` \u2014 the year segment now uses `FiscalYear.shortYearOf(...)` (the membership identifier's year is now the fiscal year).\n- Added `getFiscalYear()` \u2014 returns the `FY<YY>` label from the business-day-adjusted registration date; MapStruct auto-maps it into `OwnerDto` by name.\n- Refreshed the relevant Javadoc.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `fiscalYear` field to the `Owner` schema (so the DTO is generated) and updated the `membershipNumber`/`membershipPoints` descriptions to reflect the fiscal-year basis.\n\nEach piece stays in its own small unit: `FiscalYear` owns the date\u2192fiscal-year rule, `Tenure` reuses it for the tenure boundary, and `Owner` reuses both for its derived getters \u2014 no logic duplicated.\n\n**Result:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 BUILD SUCCESS, `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsFiscalYear` passes (`fiscalYear` = `FY26` for a `2026-09-17` registration).\n\nOne design decision worth flagging: the spec says `FY<YY>` without pinning whether `YY` is the fiscal year's **starting** or **ending** calendar year, and no test distinguishes them. I chose the **starting** year (a July-2026 date \u2192 `FY26`), keeping it directly tied to \"the fiscal year starts on 1 July.\" If your convention is the ending year (July-2026 \u2192 `FY27`), it's a one-line change in `FiscalYear.startingYearOf`/`shortYearOf` and both the label and membership number follow automatically.",
